From 5ee16beda2ad4ecf2a92f55e2184a25648adedeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hangxiang Ma <hangxiang.ma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:19:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 188/194] media: qcom: camss: Adapt SM8750 capture to separate
 AUP and RUP

Bring the Qualcomm SM8750 v6 CSID980/resource implementation forward to the
reviewed v24 address-update hooks. Reuse the v24 VFE implementation with
980 full/lite bus offsets and SM8750-supported CAMNOC clock rates. Retain
shared CPAS AHB/AXI clocks as runtime-PM clocks and use six external PHYs.
No board camera node is enabled; TPG and sensor integration are separate.

Local adaptations:
- Use independent address/register update hooks and per-path command masks.
  A lite RUP write must not repeat AUP; another path's pending shadow bit
  must not consume this path's buffer again.
- Issue two initial AUPs then one RUP after configuration. Stream-off issues
  no AUP. Require two queued buffers on SM8750 so those initial requests
  correspond to the two populated hardware slots.
- Fix the lite per-RDI IRQ stride and enable/clear RUP interrupts at both
  path and top level, verified against stock CSID980/lite880 register data.
- Preserve SM8750 full/lite offsets; do not borrow1080 register addresses.
  CAMNOC rates are limited to the existing SM8750 CAMCC table's400MHz max.

Original patches:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260721-add-support-for-camss-on-sm8750-v6-3-a5f841061d18@oss.qualcomm.com/
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260721-add-support-for-camss-on-sm8750-v6-5-a5f841061d18@oss.qualcomm.com/
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260721-add-support-for-camss-on-sm8750-v6-6-a5f841061d18@oss.qualcomm.com/
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261102-kaanapali-camss-v24-10-d6b8f3f6f66f@oss.qualcomm.com/

Stock GPL reference: lenovo-basements/android_kernel_lenovo_sm8750-modules
at e1f324632d70b2427751820cd48eefc45baab0ce.

Validation: ARM64 GCC14.2 W=1 combined CAMSS object; checkpatch; actual CSID
C code with fake MMIO matches stock per-path registers/masks for13 single-
and multi-stream configurations, two start/IRQ/queue/stop cycles each.
No full-kernel build or hardware validation. Upstream Reviewed-by/Tested-by
tags are not carried over to this locally adapted implementation.

